(vector (map (:registry/operating-states (vector :intake :propose :approve :execute :audit)), (:registry/required-technologies (vector :robotics :identity :audit-ledger)), (:actor/scope-excluded-ops (vector :finalize-fabrication-decision :authorize-custody-transfer :proceed-with-fabrication-work :finalize-custody-transfer-decision :override-workshop-safety-officer-judgment :override-safety-officer-judgment)), (:actor/robotics? true), (:adr/related (vector "2799007211-cloud-itonami-isco-7211-metal-moulders-coremakers-coverage" "2799007224-cloud-itonami-isco-7224-metal-polishers-wheel-grinders-tool-sharpeners-coverage" "2799007111-cloud-itonami-isco-7111-house-builders-coverage")), (:adr/status :accepted), (:actor/scope-excluded-terms (vector "proceed with the fabrication work" "proceed with fabrication work" "authorize the custody transfer of precious materials" "authorize the custody transfer" "authorize a custody transfer" "finalize the fabrication decision" "finalize the custody transfer decision" "override the workshop safety officer's judgment" "override the safety officer's judgment" "override workshop safety officer judgment")), (:adr/id 2799007313), (:phase/rollout "{0 {:label \"read-only\", :writes #{}, :auto #{}}, 1 {:label \"assisted-logging\", :writes #{:log-inventory-record}, :auto #{}}, 2 {:label \"assisted-coordination\", :writes #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-inventory-record}, :auto #{}}, 3 {:label \"supervised-auto\", :writes #{:flag-safety-concern :schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-inventory-record}, :auto #{:schedule-crew-operation :coordinate-supply-order :log-inventory-record}}}"), (:actor/domain :manufacturing/jewellery-workshop-scheduling-logistics-coordination), (:actor/proposal-ops (vector :log-inventory-record :schedule-crew-operation :flag-safety-concern :coordinate-supply-order)), (:actor/hard-checks (vector :jeweller-verified :workshop-verified :effect-propose :op-not-allowed :scope-exclusion)), (:registry/maturity :implemented), (:actor/isco-08 "7313"), (:actor/always-escalate-ops (vector :flag-safety-concern)), (:adr/doc_type "adr"), (:operation/nodes (vector :intake :advise :govern :decide :request-approval :commit :hold)), (:operation/entry-point :intake), (:adr/body "# ADR 2799007313: cloud-itonami ISCO-08 7313 Jewellery and Precious Metal Workers workshop scheduling/logistics/inventory-logging coordination coverage\n\n## Status\n\nAccepted\n\n## Context\n\nThis is part of the occupation-classification track (sibling to the\n`cloud-itonami-isic-*` industry-actor rollout, same governing\nADR-2607121000): codify every ISCO-08 occupation unit group as an\nautonomous \"actor\" (LLM/advisor behind an independent Governor, a\n`langgraph.graph` StateGraph, append-only audit ledger), modeled on a\nrobotics premise -- a robot performs the occupation's physical/\nadministrative work, proposing actions to an independent Governor that\ngates them, never dispatches hardware itself, always escalates\nhigh-stakes decisions to a human. This ADR covers **ISCO-08 class 7313\n-- Jewellery and Precious Metal Workers** only, Wave3 (production/\ntrades) of the rollout (Wave0/1/2 100% complete, Wave3\nconstruction/metal-trades and agriculture batches already landed,\nincluding the comparable precious-materials-adjacent workshop-safety\nactor `cloud-itonami-isco-7211`).\n\nThe `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's live `{:id \"7313\" ...}` entry\nwas verified against a fresh clone before any work began (`clojure -M\n-e \"(require 'kotoba.occupation) (println (kotoba.occupation/get-occupation\n\\\"7313\\\"))\"` from a checkout with the `kotoba-lang/technology`\nsibling present at the correct `../technology` relative path), and its\n`:name` read exactly \"Jewellery and Precious Metal Workers\" --\nconfirming the premise, no mismatch. Prior to this ADR the entry's\n`:maturity` was `:spec` with `:required-technologies [:robotics\n:identity :audit-ledger]` and no `:repo`/`:business-id`; no repository\nexisted at `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7313` (`gh api` 404\nconfirmed before scaffolding). This ADR and its companion registry\nedit promote the `7313` entry to `:implemented`.\n\nJewellery and precious metal workers handle high-value precious metals\nand gemstones AND use torches/acids for soldering and finishing --\nreal physical-safety stakes (burn exposure, chemical/acid exposure)\ncombined with a chain-of-custody / high-value-materials integrity\ndimension unique to this vertical among the fleet so far. The\ncontrolling constraint for this vertical is that the closed op\nallowlist must NEVER include any op that directly finalizes a\njewellery-fabrication-execution decision, or authorizes a\nprecious-materials custody-transfer, or overrides a workshop safety\nofficer's judgment -- those decisions must always be a hard permanent\nblock or an always-escalate op, never auto-commit-eligible. This actor\nis deliberately scoped to WORKSHOP\nSCHEDULING/LOGISTICS/INVENTORY-LOGGING COORDINATION ONLY -- it never\nperforms fabrication work or authorizes material transfers itself.\n\nThe reference implementation mirrored closely for module SHAPE and the\nclosed-allowlist + independently-verified-provenance safety pattern is\n[`cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7211`](https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7211)\n(Metal Moulders and Coremakers: `store`/`advisor`/`governor`/`actor`\nsplit, `langgraph.graph` StateGraph, full doc set, same wave, a\ncomparable precious-materials-adjacent workshop-safety pattern already\nlanded and independently re-tested at the start of this session) --\ncloned and read in full in this session.\n\n## Decision\n\nPublish `cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7313` as an OSS jewellery\nworkshop scheduling/logistics/inventory-logging coordination actor for\njewellery and precious metal workers, following the SAME\ngoverned-actor architecture as every prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*`\nactor in this fleet: **Jewellery Workshop Coordination Advisor ⊣\nJewelCoordGovernor** on a `langgraph.graph` StateGraph\n(`io.github.kotoba-lang/langgraph`, git-sha-pinned identically to the\nreference's `deps.edn` -- a different library coordinate from the\n`langgraph-clj` used by the unrelated `20-actors/*` actor family),\nwith an independent Governor, human-in-the-loop approval via\n`interrupt-before`, and an append-only audit ledger.\n\nThis actor is deliberately **workshop scheduling/logistics/\ninventory-logging coordination ONLY, never direct fabrication or\ncustody-transfer authority** -- it must NEVER be designed to exercise,\nsimulate exercising, or propose exercising a\njewellery-fabrication-execution decision, a precious-materials\ncustody-transfer authorization, or any override of a workshop safety\nofficer's judgment. These are not merely gated behind escalation --\nthey are structurally absent from the op-allowlist entirely.\n\n### Closed proposal-op allowlist (all `:effect :propose`)\n\n- `:log-inventory-record` -- precious-material/finished-piece\n  inventory data logging (metadata only, NEVER a transfer\n  authorization)\n- `:schedule-crew-operation` -- crew/task scheduling proposal\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- surface a burn-exposure/chemical-exposure/\n  custody-discrepancy concern, ALWAYS escalates, NEVER auto-commit\n  eligible\n- `:coordinate-supply-order` -- non-precious materials/tools\n  procurement proposal\n\nThis actor has **NO op, anywhere in its allowlist, that resembles** a\njewellery-fabrication-execution decision or a precious-materials\ncustody-transfer authorization or a workshop-safety-officer-judgment\noverride. These are **structurally absent from the op-allowlist\nentirely**, not merely gated behind escalation -- an op such as\n`:finalize-fabrication-decision` cannot even be proposed by the\nreference mock advisor (its `infer`/`rationale-for` functions only\never emit one of the four allowlist ops), and if any code path (a\nforged proposal, a future LLM advisor, a misbehaving fork) ever\nproduced such an op, the governor's closed-allowlist HARD check\n(`:unknown-op`) rejects it unconditionally and permanently. A second,\nindependent HARD check (`:scope-excluded-action`) names six\nconcretely-forbidden ops (`jewelcoord.governor/scope-excluded-ops`:\n`:finalize-fabrication-decision`, `:authorize-custody-transfer`,\n`:proceed-with-fabrication-work`, `:finalize-custody-transfer-decision`,\n`:override-workshop-safety-officer-judgment`,\n`:override-safety-officer-judgment`) as defense-in-depth, and is\nverified by dedicated unit tests\n(`jewelcoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-fabrication-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-custody-transfer`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-fabrication-work`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-workshop-safety-officer-judgment`).\n\n### Four HARD governor checks (permanent, un-overridable)\n\n1. **Jeweller unregistered** -- any proposal must resolve to an\n   independently registered jeweller record (`:no-jeweller`). Never\n   trusts the proposal's own claim of who the crew member is.\n2. **Workshop unregistered** -- any proposal must cite an\n   independently registered workshop site (`:no-workshop`). Together\n   with check 1, this directly implements the CRITICAL invariant that\n   a worker/workshop record must be independently verified/registered\n   before any action.\n3. **Effect not `:propose`** -- any other `:effect` value is a HARD\n   block (a claim to directly actuate outside governance)\n   (`:no-actuation`).\n4. **Op not allowed / scope-excluded action** -- any `:op` outside the\n   closed four-op allowlist is a HARD, PERMANENT block (`:unknown-op`),\n   and independently, any proposal whose `:op` names one of the six\n   concretely-forbidden ops above, OR whose free-text `:rationale`\n   names a finalization/execution action for proceeding with\n   fabrication work, authorizing a custody transfer, or overriding a\n   workshop safety officer's judgment, is a second HARD, PERMANENT\n   block (`:scope-excluded-action`), evaluated unconditionally on\n   content -- defense-in-depth on top of the allowlist check: even if\n   a future change somehow widened the allowlist, content-based\n   rejection still independently blocks fabrication-execution/\n   custody-transfer/safety-override language wherever it appears in\n   free text.\n\n### One always-escalate (SOFT) gate, one threshold gate, plus the general confidence floor\n\n- `:flag-safety-concern` -- ALWAYS escalates to a human, regardless of\n  confidence (governor's implicit always-risky check). This is the\n  ONLY channel by which the robot may surface a burn-exposure/\n  chemical-exposure/custody-discrepancy observation -- it never\n  resolves the concern itself, and the robot's role ends at \"here is\n  the hazard/discrepancy data,\" never \"here is what I recommend doing\n  about workshop safety or custody.\"\n- a `:coordinate-supply-order` proposal whose `:cost` exceeds\n  `supply-cost-threshold` (2000, inclusive boundary verified by\n  `ok-supply-order-at-threshold-boundary`) -- always needs human\n  sign-off, independent of confidence. This is an ESCALATION, not a\n  hard block, per the task's explicit domain design: an over-threshold\n  non-precious materials/tools order is not itself unsafe, unlike a\n  fabrication-execution, custody-transfer, or safety-officer-override\n  attempt, which is why it is handled by a different mechanism (soft\n  escalate vs. structural absence).\n- (advisor confidence below `confidence-floor` 0.6 also escalates, for\n  any op.)\n\n### Self-trip guard (fleet-known bug class, carried over from the sibling ISIC/ISCO tracks)\n\nA governor's scope-exclusion term list phrased as a bare noun (e.g.\n\"fabrication\", \"gold\", \"custody\") can accidentally match inside the\nmock advisor's own default rationale text for a legitimate proposal,\nself-blocking the actor's own happy path -- this is exactly the risk\nthis vertical's own vocabulary (a workshop coordination actor working\nadjacent to fabrication and precious-materials custody necessarily\ndiscusses those concepts to do its scheduling/logging job) could\ntrigger if phrased carelessly. `jewelcoord.governor/scope-excluded-phrases`\nis phrased exclusively as finalization/execution ACTIONS (e.g.\n\"proceed with the fabrication work\", \"authorize the custody transfer\nof precious materials\", \"override the workshop safety officer's\njudgment\" -- matching the task's own worked example phrasing), never\nbare nouns, and\n`jewelcoord.governor-test/default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-on-scope-exclusion`\nis a dedicated regression test asserting every op in the closed\nallowlist, driven through the default mock advisor, never trips\n`:scope-excluded-action`. The mock advisor's own default rationale\ntemplate was deliberately written to contain the bare nouns (\"logged\ninventory record for jeweller ...\", \"scheduled crew operation for\nfinishing task ...\", \"... routed for workshop safety officer review\")\nWITHOUT containing any of the full finalization-action phrases, and\nthe regression test's request fixture additionally includes the task\n\"routine gold custody finishing task\" to stress-test the bare-noun\n(\"gold\", \"custody\") vs. action-phrase distinction directly, so the\nregression test is a genuine stress test, not a vacuous pass. Green on\nfirst run in this session -- the scope-exclusion self-trip guard\nitself was never tripped during development.\n`jewelcoord.actor-test/holds-a-scope-excluded-op-even-at-high-confidence`\nand `.../holds-a-custody-transfer-authorization-even-at-high-confidence`\nadditionally exercise the same invariant through the full graph run,\nconfirming a scope-excluded proposal never reaches `commit-record!`\nregardless of disposition path.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry's `{:id \"7313\" ...}` entry\n  promoted from `:spec` to `:implemented`, with `:repo`/`:business-id`\n  set to the real repository\n  (`https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7313` /\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-7313`), and `maturity-summary`'s implemented\n  count bumped accordingly (recomputed live from the registry via\n  `kotoba.occupation/maturity-summary`, not assumed, immediately\n  before the edit).\n- Full test suite (`clojure -M:test`): 23 tests, 50 assertions, 0\n  failures, 0 errors -- raw output captured in this ADR's\n  `:test/counts` and in the task report, independently re-verified\n  against a brand-new fresh clone of the pushed repository (not just\n  the local working copy).\n- No `manifest/west.yml` changes -- this actor is registered purely via\n  the `kotoba-lang/occupation` capability registry, consistent with\n  sibling `cloud-itonami-isco-*`/`cloud-itonami-isic-*` actors.\n- No `kotoba-lang/technology` dependency was added to the actor's\n  `deps.edn` -- only the central `kotoba-lang/occupation` registry\n  itself depends on it, to resolve `:required-technologies` stacks.\n- This ADR is EDN-only, matching the live `90-docs/adr` convention\n  (commit `6d2d0eeda658`, \"Remove all .md, normalize ADRs to\n  tx-data\") -- a single-entity EDN vector with an `:adr/body` string\n  blob rather than a paired `.md`+`.edn`.\n\n## Alternatives considered\n\n- Giving the actor an op like `:approve-custody-transfer` that is\n  merely gated behind an always-escalate list (the shape\n  `cloud-itonami-isco-3313` uses for `:approve-over-ceiling-posting`):\n  rejected outright per the task's explicit domain-design guidance --\n  an always-escalate op still means the *capability* to authorize a\n  precious-materials custody transfer exists in the code path and is\n  merely deferred to a human gate. For a decision this severe\n  (high-value precious metals/gemstones chain-of-custody, plus burn/\n  chemical-exposure physical-safety stakes), the capability itself\n  must not exist. The only op related to safety/custody escalation is\n  `:flag-safety-concern`, which surfaces the need for human/workshop-\n  safety-officer attention and never itself decides, authorizes, or\n  defers a fabrication-execution or custody-transfer decision for\n  later automatic execution.\n- Making the supply-cost ceiling a HARD block (mirroring the 3313\n  reference's transaction-amount-ceiling HARD check): rejected per the\n  task's explicit domain design -- an over-threshold non-precious\n  materials/tools order is not itself unsafe, so it is handled as a\n  soft escalate gate, not a hard block; only the\n  fabrication-execution/custody-transfer/safety-officer-override class\n  is a hard, unconditional block.\n- A bare-noun scope-exclusion term list (e.g. `[\"fabrication\" \"gold\"\n  \"custody\"]`): rejected outright per the fleet-known self-trip bug\n  class described above (and CLAUDE.md's own worked example for this\n  exact task), and per the explicit instruction to phrase\n  scope-exclusion terms as finalization/execution ACTIONS, never bare\n  nouns -- this actor's own domain necessarily discusses fabrication/\n  gold/custody/safety-officer concepts to do its scheduling/logging\n  job, so a bare-noun list would risk self-blocking the actor's own\n  legitimate proposals (regression-tested directly against rationale\n  text and a request `:task` that deliberately contain those bare\n  nouns).\n- Naming the excluded-op set after \"workshop safety officer\" only, vs.\n  also naming a second distinct authority figure for custody (e.g. a\n  separate \"custodian\" role): rejected -- the task's domain design\n  names a workshop-safety-officer's judgment and a\n  precious-materials-custody-transfer authorization as two distinct\n  hard-blocked ACTION classes, not two distinct human authority roles\n  to model separately; `:authorize-custody-transfer` /\n  `:finalize-custody-transfer-decision` cover the custody class and\n  `:override-workshop-safety-officer-judgment` /\n  `:override-safety-officer-judgment` cover the safety-officer class,\n  fully covering the specified scope without inventing an unspecified\n  second authority role.\n- Merging `jeweller` and `workshop` into a single entity (only\n  checking one provenance record): rejected -- the two-entity\n  provenance shape (independently-registered jeweller AND\n  independently-registered workshop) matches the CRITICAL invariant\n  that a \"worker/workshop record must be independently\n  verified/registered before any action\" and the established pattern\n  from prior `cloud-itonami-isco-*` actors with two-sided provenance\n  checks.\n\n## Itemized safety confirmation\n\nEvery op in this actor's closed proposal-op allowlist, and why it is\nsafe under the constraints above:\n\n1. **`:log-inventory-record`** -- precious-material/finished-piece\n   inventory data logging only, metadata-only and NEVER a transfer\n   authorization. Requires an independently registered jeweller AND\n   workshop (`:no-jeweller`/`:no-workshop`). Not a\n   jewellery-fabrication-execution decision or a custody-transfer\n   authorization in any respect -- it is a records-management action.\n2. **`:schedule-crew-operation`** -- crew/task scheduling proposal\n   only. Cannot carry a jewellery-fabrication-execution decision or a\n   custody-transfer authorization (structurally absent from the op's\n   field shape; any such attempt via free text is caught by the\n   `:scope-excluded-action` content check). Does not authorize,\n   finalize, or draw any conclusion about specific fabrication work or\n   material custody -- it is a calendar/logistics action.\n3. **`:flag-safety-concern`** -- surfaces a burn-exposure/chemical-\n   exposure/custody-discrepancy concern to a human/workshop safety\n   officer; ALWAYS escalates, unconditionally, at every confidence\n   level, NEVER auto-commit eligible. This is the ONLY channel through\n   which a safety or custody-discrepancy observation may be surfaced,\n   and it explicitly never resolves, decides, or acts on anything\n   itself -- the workshop safety officer (and, for custody\n   discrepancies, an independently verified custody chain) reviews and\n   acts entirely on their own authority.\n4. **`:coordinate-supply-order`** -- non-precious materials/tools\n   procurement proposal only (item, cost). Not a\n   jewellery-fabrication-execution decision or a custody-transfer\n   authorization of any kind -- it is a purchasing-logistics action,\n   gated by ordinary cost-ceiling escalation (above 2000 always\n   escalates).\n\nNo op in this allowlist, and no op anywhere in this codebase, resembles\na jewellery-fabrication-execution decision (e.g. proceeding with\nspecific fabrication work), a precious-materials custody-transfer\nauthorization, or a workshop-safety-officer-judgment override -- these\ncategories are structurally absent, not gated, confirmed by: (a) the\nclosed four-op allowlist itself (`jewelcoord.governor/allowed-ops`),\n(b) six concretely-named forbidden-op fixtures rejected at the\ngovernor-unit level (`jewelcoord.governor/scope-excluded-ops`,\n`jewelcoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-op-finalize-fabrication-decision`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-authorize-custody-transfer`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-proceed-with-fabrication-work`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-op-override-workshop-safety-officer-judgment`),\nand (c) a content-based scope-exclusion check independent of the `:op`\nfield (`jewelcoord.governor/scope-excluded-phrases`,\n`.../contains-excluded-phrase?`), tested directly against a rationale\nthat attempts to proceed with fabrication work, authorize a custody\ntransfer, or override a workshop safety officer's judgment even via an\notherwise-allowlisted op\n(`jewelcoord.governor-test/hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-even-with-allowlisted-op`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-authorize-custody-transfer`,\n`.../hard-on-scope-excluded-rationale-override-workshop-safety-officer`).\n"), (:adr/date "2026-07-18"), (:actor/cost-threshold-escalate-ops "{:coordinate-supply-order 2000}"), (:test/counts "{:total 23, :assertions 50, :failures 0, :errors 0}"), (:actor/coordination? true), (:actor/name "Jewellery Workshop Scheduling and Logistics Coordination Practice"), (:db/id -1), (:test/coverage (vector :governor-hard-checks :advisor-shapes :integration :store-contract :scope-exclusion-self-trip-regression :jeweller-verification :workshop-verification :closed-op-allowlist :supply-cost-threshold-escalation)), (:registry/business-id "cloud-itonami-isco-7313"), (:registry/repo "https://github.com/cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7313"), (:adr/scope (vector :kotoba-lang/occupation :cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isco-7313)), (:test/simulator :jewelcoord.actor-test), (:adr/title "cloud-itonami-isco-7313 — Jewellery and Precious Metal Workers Workshop Scheduling/Logistics/Inventory-Logging Coordination Coverage"), (:adr/source-format "edn"), (:adr/references (vector 2607121000)), (:actor/id :cloud-itonami-isco-7313)))